.\" Comprehensive manpage for the powerliners binary suite (5 binaries).
.\" Contact https://github.com/MenkeTechnologies/powerliners to correct errors or omissions.
.TH POWERLINEALL 1 "2026-10-08" "powerliners 0.2.32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
powerlineall \- comprehensive reference for the powerliners 5-binary suite (powerline / powerline-daemon / powerline-config / powerline-render / powerline-lint)
.SH OVERVIEW
.B powerliners
is a 1:1 Rust port of the upstream Python
.B powerline-status
project. It ships five cooperating binaries that together replace the
entire Python implementation while preserving the existing
.B ~/.config/powerline/
JSON config tree byte-for-byte.
.PP
This manpage documents the suite as a whole: invocation order, wire
protocol between client and daemon, config-lookup cascade, theme
grammar, segment dispatch, and the rendering pipeline. For individual
binaries see the
.BR powerline (1)
page; the other four binaries are documented here and by their
.B \-\-help
screens.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B powerline
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\fIEXT\fR
[\fISIDE\fR]
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.PP
.B powerline-daemon
[\fB\-f\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR]
[\fB\-k\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.PP
.B powerline-render
\fIEXT\fR
[\fISIDE\fR]
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.PP
.B powerline-config
{\fBtmux\fR | \fBshell\fR | \fBvim\fR}
\fIACTION\fR
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.PP
.B powerline-lint
\fB\-p\fR \fIPATH\fR
[\fB\-d\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SH "1.  ARCHITECTURE"
.B powerliners
splits the rendering pipeline into a long-lived daemon and a thin
fork-on-demand client:
.IP \(bu 2
.B powerline-daemon
\(em a single Unix-socket server per UID. Loads the JSON config tree
once, instantiates segment classes once, holds the theme dictionaries
and color palettes in memory.
.IP \(bu 2
.B powerline
\(em the lightweight client. Forwards \fIargv\fR + \fIcwd\fR + the
environment to the daemon over a Unix socket and copies the rendered
statusline to stdout. Falls back to
.B powerline-render
when the daemon is unreachable.
.IP \(bu 2
.B powerline-render
\(em the direct-render fallback. Same render path as the daemon but
no socket; pays the full config-load cost on every invocation.
.IP \(bu 2
.B powerline-config
\(em config helper. Used by shell, tmux and vim init to deduce the
client command, gate optional components, run tmux setup, and locate the
bundled vim plugin.
.IP \(bu 2
.B powerline-lint
\(em static-analysis tool. Checks the structure of the colorscheme and
theme JSON files (see
.BR LINTING ).
.SH "2.  WIRE PROTOCOL"
The
.B powerline
client and the
.B powerline-daemon
server communicate over an abstract or filesystem Unix socket. The
wire format mirrors the upstream C client
.RB ( vendor/powerline/client/powerline.c
lines 126\-148):
.PP
.RS
.nf
hex(argc-1) "\\0" argv[0] "\\0" argv[1] "\\0" ... cwd "\\0" env[0] "\\0" ... "\\0\\0"
.fi
.RE
.PP
The server demarshals the request, dispatches to the appropriate
.B Powerline.<ext>
extension, and writes the rendered byte stream back. Cross\(hyversion
clients and servers interop as long as the wire format is preserved.
.SH "3.  SOCKET PATHS"
.TP
.B /tmp/powerline-ipc-<uid>
Filesystem socket (macOS, FreeBSD, OpenBSD, NetBSD).
.TP
.B \\0powerline-ipc-<uid>
Abstract socket (Linux). Has no filesystem entry; appears only in
.BR ss (8) " -x"
and
.BR lsof (8) " -U"
under the leading NUL marker. Survives
.B /tmp
cleanup races.
.PP
Both can be overridden with
.B \-\-socket
.IR PATH .
.SH "4.  CONFIG CASCADE"
.B powerline-render
and
.B powerline-daemon
load
.B config.json
+ theme JSON from the following roots. Later roots override earlier
ones:
.IP 1. 4
The bundled defaults compiled into the
.B powerliners
binaries themselves \(em embedded from
.B src/ported/config_files/
via
.B include_str!
and extracted on first use to
.BR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/powerliners/config_files/
(default
.BR ~/.cache/powerliners/config_files/ ).
.IP 2. 4
Each directory in
.B $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS
(suffixed
.BR /powerline ).
No system directory is searched when it is unset.
.IP 3. 4
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/powerline/
(falls back to
.BR ~/.config/powerline/ ).
.PP
When
.B $POWERLINE_CONFIG_PATHS
is set and non-empty, its colon-separated directories replace this
whole list.
.PP
Per-key merging follows the upstream Python
.B mergedicts
semantics: deep dictionary merge, REMOVE sentinel for explicit deletion,
nested\(hylist append.
.SH "5.  THEME GRAMMAR"
A theme JSON file declares
.IR segments :
left / right list of segment specs, each segment naming a Python\(hystyle
.B segment_data
function (mapped in the Rust port to a dispatch table of
.B fn(args: &Map<String, Value>, info: &Map<String, Value>) -> Option<Value>
adapters). The segment returns a list of
.B highlight_groups
+ contents tuples. The theme's
.B segment_data
section can override
.B args ,
.BR contents ,
.BR before / after ,
or the
.B priority
for any segment by key.
.PP
Color palettes live in
.BR colors.json ;
named colors are referenced from
.B colorschemes/<ext>/<name>.json
which maps highlight\(hygroup names to
.B fg / bg / attrs
triples. The theme grammar is the same as upstream and any existing
.B ~/.config/powerline/
tree works unchanged.
.SH "6.  SEGMENT DISPATCH"
Segments fall into three categories:
.TP
.B common
Cross\(hyextension segments (battery, network, weather, mail, hostname,
cwd, vcs branch). Located under
.BR src/ported/segments/common/ .
.TP
.B shell
Shell\(hyspecific segments (
.BR last_status ,
.BR last_pipe_status ,
.BR jobnum ,
.BR mode ,
.BR continuation ).
.TP
.B tmux
Tmux\(hyspecific segments (
.BR attached_clients ).
.PP
The
.B player
segment family additionally supports per-player adapters (spotify, itunes,
mocp, mpd, cmus, rhythmbox, clementine) through a common
.B PlayerSegment
base, faithfully mirroring upstream's class hierarchy.
.SH "7.  DAEMON LIFECYCLE"
.B powerline-daemon
defaults to forking into the background after binding the socket
.RB ( "powerline-daemon -q"
in
.BR ~/.profile ).
On
.B SIGTERM
it unlinks its pidfile (non\(hyLinux platforms only) and exits with
status 1; on
.B SIGINT
it exits with status 0. Config files are re\(hystat'd on each request and
reloaded when a modification time changed, unless
.B common.reload_config
is false; no signal is needed.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreground
keeps the daemon attached to the terminal (useful for systemd
.B Type=simple
units).
.IP \(bu 2
.BR \-r ", " \-\-replace
kills any existing daemon on the same socket and takes over.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR \-k ", " \-\-kill
sends the daemon an EOF marker over its socket, which makes it shut down,
and exits (status 1 if no daemon is running; it cannot be combined with
.B \-\-foreground
or
.BR \-\-replace ).
.IP \(bu 2
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
suppresses the "already running" notice when another daemon already
holds the socket, and the
.B \-\-kill
and
.B \-\-replace
status messages.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " " \fIPATH\fR
binds the given socket path instead of the default.
.SS Render isolation
The event loop never renders. Requests are dispatched to a worker pool
.RB ( POWERLINERS_RENDER_THREADS ,
default 4) and completions are collected through a self\(hypipe in the
loop's poll set, so a slow request cannot delay another client's. Three
bounds keep a misbehaving segment contained:
.IP \(bu 2
Each segment gets 2000\ ms by default, overridable per segment with a
.B "\(dqtimeout\(dq:"
.I ms
key in the theme. A segment that overruns is served from its last good
value (up to 60\ s old) and is not re\(hyentered until the overdue call
returns.
.IP \(bu 2
Segments that shell out kill any child that outlives its budget, so a
wedged helper cannot pin a worker.
.IP \(bu 2
Connections are reaped after 10\ s regardless of state, and immediately
when the client hangs up. Accepted sockets carry send/receive timeouts.
.PP
Watchdog trips and connection reaps are recorded in
.BR ~/.powerliners/powerliners.log .
.SH "8.  INVOCATION FROM SHELLS"
.SS zsh
.RS
.nf
function powerline_precmd() {
    PS1="$(powerline shell left \\
        --last-exit-code=$? \\
        --jobnum=$(jobs -p | wc -l))"
}
precmd_functions+=(powerline_precmd)
.fi
.RE
.SS bash
.RS
.nf
PROMPT_COMMAND='PS1="$(powerline shell left \\
    --last-exit-code=$? \\
    --jobnum=$(jobs -p | wc -l))"'
.fi
.RE
.SS tmux
.RS
.nf
set -g status-interval 2
set -g status-left  "#(powerline tmux left)"
set -g status-right "#(powerline tmux right)"
set -g status-style "bg=colour234,fg=colour231"
.fi
.RE
.SS vim
.RS
.nf
if executable('powerline-config')
  execute 'source' trim(system('powerline-config vim source-path'))
endif
.fi
.RE
Vim integration needs no Python at all. The
.B powerline.vim
plugin is embedded in the binary via
.BR include_str! ;
.B powerline-config vim source-path
extracts it to
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME/powerliners/vim/powerline.vim
(default
.BR ~/.cache/powerliners/vim/ )
and prints the path, which the
.B :execute 'source'
line then sources. The plugin is vim8\(hycompatible syntax only and
works on vim 7.4+, vim 9, and neovim; it sets
.B laststatus=2
itself and shells out to the
.B powerline
client on each refresh.
.SH "9.  CONFIG INTROSPECTION"
.B powerline-config
subcommands:
.TP
.B tmux setup
Source the bundled tmux configuration into the running server and set
the environment it needs \(em the canonical
.B run-shell
line for
.BR ~/.tmux.conf .
Install\(hymethod agnostic: the embedded
.B powerline-base.conf
plus the version\(hymatched
.B powerline_tmux_*.conf
variants are extracted to
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME/powerliners/tmux/
(default
.BR ~/.cache/powerliners/tmux/ )
on first call, then sourced. A
.B status\-left\-length
or
.B status\-right\-length
that differs from tmux's own default is read before sourcing and
re\(hyapplied afterwards, so re\(hyrunning setup against a live server
does not revert it to the
.BR powerline\-base.conf " values (20 / 150)."
.TP
.B tmux source
.TQ
.B tmux setenv
Accepted but not implemented as standalone actions: they print an error
and exit 1. Use
.B tmux setup
instead, which performs both steps.
.TP
.B shell command
Print the deduced client command, suitable for
.BR $POWERLINE_COMMAND ;
exit 1 if none is found.
.TP
.B "shell uses COMPONENT" " [" \-s " " \fISHELL\fR ]
Exit 0 iff
.I COMPONENT
.RB ( tmux " or " prompt )
is enabled for the current configuration (\fBext.shell.components\fR in
.BR config.json ,
default both) and neither
.B POWERLINE_NO_<SHELL>_<COMPONENT>
nor
.B POWERLINE_NO_SHELL_<COMPONENT>
is set to a non\(hyempty value. Used to gate optional binding setup during
shell init.
.TP
.B vim source-path
Extract the bundled
.B powerline.vim
plugin to
.B $XDG_CACHE_HOME/powerliners/vim/
and print its path. Non\(hyupstream subcommand \(em it exists because
the Rust port ships the vim plugin inside the binary instead of a
site\(hypackages directory.
.SH "10.  LINTING"
.B powerline-lint
requires at least one
.BR \-p " " \fIPATH\fR
(long form
.BR \-\-config\-path ;
repeatable) and scans the
.B colorschemes/
and
.B themes/
trees under those paths. It reports:
.IP \(bu 2
Files that fail to parse, or whose root is not a JSON object.
.IP \(bu 2
File names that start or end with
.B __
(other than
.BR __main__ ).
.IP \(bu 2
Colorschemes missing
.BR groups ;
groups that are neither an alias string nor an object with
.B fg
and
.BR bg ;
.B attrs
not a list;
.B mode_translations
not an object.
.IP \(bu 2
Themes missing
.BR segments ;
.BR segments.left / right / above
not arrays; non\(hyinteger
.BR spaces ,
.BR outer_padding ,
.BR cursor_columns ;
non\(hynumeric
.BR cursor_space .
.PP
Segment function names, color references, format strings and
.B config.json
/
.B colors.json
are not checked.
.SH "11.  ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
.B POWERLINE_COMMAND
The command invoked by shell + tmux integrations. Set to
.B powerline
to use this native binary.
.B "powerline-config tmux setup"
publishes it into the tmux server environment
.I before
sourcing the config files, because from tmux 2.1 on
.B status-left
expands it at source time rather than at
.B #()
run time.
.TP
.B POWERLINE_CONFIG_PATHS
Colon\(hyseparated config search roots; when non\(hyempty, replaces the
default cascade (see CONFIG CASCADE).
.TP
.B POWERLINE_CONFIG_OVERRIDES
Main\(hyconfig
.B key=value
overrides, merged with
.BR \-c / \-\-config\-override .
.TP
.B POWERLINE_THEME_OVERRIDES
Theme
.B key=value
overrides, merged with
.BR \-t / \-\-theme\-override .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_DIRS
System config roots (each suffixed
.BR /powerline ).
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Extraction root for the bundled config, tmux and vim files; falls back to
.BR ~/.cache .
.TP
.B POWERLINE_RESET_FIFO
Path to the per\(hyshell FIFO used by the Reactive Prompt Push
extension. Exported by
.B _powerline_reactive_setup
and forwarded to the daemon, which writes a wake byte to it when a
watched prompt input (cwd,
.BR .git/HEAD ,
.BR .git/index ,
the active branch ref) changes.
.TP
.B POWERLINERS_RENDER_THREADS
Size of the daemon's render worker pool (default 4). Renders never run
on the event\(hyloop thread, so this bounds how many client requests can
be rendered at once, not whether the loop stays responsive.
.TP
.B POWERLINERS_ICONS
Selects the icon tier for the bundled
.B src/extensions/
segments:
unset \(em Nerd Font glyphs;
.B unicode
\(em text\(hypresentation Unicode fallbacks;
.B ascii
\(em label\(hystyle ASCII for non\(hyUTF8 terminals.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
User config root; falls back to
.B ~/.config
if unset.
.SH "12.  FILES"
.TP
.B ~/.config/powerline/config.json
User config root.
.TP
.B ~/.config/powerline/themes/<ext>/<name>.json
Per\(hyextension theme JSON files.
.TP
.B ~/.config/powerline/colorschemes/<ext>/<name>.json
Highlight\(hygroup color mappings.
.TP
.B ~/.config/powerline/colors.json
Named color palette.
.TP
.B /tmp/powerline-ipc-<uid>
Daemon Unix socket (macOS / BSD).
.TP
.B \\0powerline-ipc-<uid>
Daemon Unix socket (Linux abstract).
.TP
.B ~/.powerliners/powerliners.log
Diagnostic log written by the daemon and renderers.
.TP
.B /tmp/powerline-ipc-<uid>.pid
Daemon pidfile (macOS / BSD).
.SH "13.  EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Successful render (
.B powerline ,
.BR powerline-render ).
.TP
.B 0
Daemon started successfully (
.BR powerline-daemon ).
.TP
.B 0
Lint clean (
.BR powerline-lint ).
.TP
.B 1
No argument given, or daemon unreachable AND fallback failed (
.BR powerline ).
.TP
.B 1
Daemon already running, or no daemon to kill (
.BR powerline-daemon ).
.TP
.B 1
Lint problems found (
.BR powerline-lint ).
.TP
.B 2
Missing or unknown argument (
.BR powerline-lint ,
.BR powerline-config ,
.BR powerline-render ).
.SH "14.  PERFORMANCE NOTES"
The Python upstream pays an interpreter import cost on every
render. Because tmux re\(hyrenders the statusline at
.B status-interval
and shell prompts re\(hyrender on every keystroke (with
.B precmd
hooks fired), the import tax compounds into a noticeable interactive
latency.
.PP
.B powerliners
has no interpreter import step and no GIL. With a warm
.B powerline-daemon
the per\(hyrender cost is dominated by the socket roundtrip. Without the
daemon,
.B powerline-render
pays the config\(hyload cost on every invocation.
